{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22316 - PROTEIN:5793",
  "verbalization": "Calenduloside C appears to exert its biological effects through a shared mechanism of action, targeting the VMRC-LCP protein, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including S-ethylcysteine zwitterion and Cocosamide B. These compounds all ultimately lead to a target in hepatocytes, suggesting a potential role for VMRC-LCP in mediating the toxic or regulatory effects of Calenduloside C on liver cells. The evidence indicates that Calenduloside C may act through a common pathway, where the VMRC-LCP serves as a critical intermediate, possibly modulating cellular processes that influence hepatocyte function. The consistent targeting of VMRC-LCP by different compounds supports the idea of a shared molecular mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction between Calenduloside C and VMRC-LCP remains to be elucidated.",
